# Observability gate — Sentry faults, PostHog outcomes

**Non-negotiable:** a new or changed feature must answer two questions in the same change.
"Forgot" is not an answer.

| Question                                          | If yes                                                                                                           | If no                                 |
| ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Does it produce a **fault** an engineer must fix? | Make sure it reaches a choke point (below), or call `captureError` / `captureSentryException` if it is swallowed | Mark `sentry: N/A` with the reason    |
| Does the user **do** something worth measuring?   | Add the event to **both** catalogs and emit it once                                                              | Mark `analytics: N/A` with the reason |

## Faults (Sentry)

Captured **once**, at a shared seam. Do not add a second capture at the call site.

| Runtime | Seam                                                                               |
| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Edge    | `handleEdgeError`, `serveCronPost`, `withEdgeErrorCapture`                         |
| Edge    | `captureSideEffectFailure` for a side effect that fails after the request          |
| Browser | `AppErrorBoundary` / `RouteErrorFallback`, TanStack `QueryCache` / `MutationCache` |
| Browser | `adminEdgeFetch` / `callEdgeFunction` / `publicEdgeFetch`                          |
| Browser | `captureError` for a swallowed failure nothing else sees                           |

- An expected result is **not** a fault: validation, a blocked captcha, an anti-spam block, a
  404, a deliberate 4xx `EdgeError`, an offline request, an aborted request.
- No PII. `user.id` only, no email, no IP, no message bodies, no capability-token query
  values. The scrub list is `ui/src/lib/telemetry/scrub.ts` + `_shared/telemetryScrub.ts`
  (a parity test keeps them identical).
- Fingerprint anything that can repeat (`['edge', fn, statusBucket]`), so one broken
  endpoint is one issue and not thousands.

## Outcomes (PostHog)

- Name: `object_action`, snake_case, past tense. Declared in `ui/src/lib/posthog/catalog.ts`
  **and** `_shared/posthogCatalog.ts` when emitted server-side; `catalogParity.test.ts`
  fails otherwise.
- Server-decided outcomes emit on the **edge after the write succeeds**. Browser is for
  intent and UI-only steps. Never both.
- Properties: ids, enums, counts, booleans, buckets. No free text, names, emails, phones,
  URLs with query strings. Money as `amount_bucket`.
- **Never** `captureException` / `$exception` in PostHog. There is no helper for it, and
  `scripts/dev/check-posthog-analytics-only.sh` fails CI if one appears.

## Scheduled work

A new cron must be listed in `_shared/systemHealth/jobsRegistry.ts` so it appears on
`/admin/health`. Sentry cron monitors are limited to **one** on the current plan
(`sd-refund-cron`); see `_shared/sentryCron.ts`.

## Verify

- `bun run check:posthog-analytics-only`
- `bun run check:sentry-imports`
- `bun run test` (catalog parity, scrub parity)

Live drill: `docs/guides/testing/observability-manual.md`.

